 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you doing? Definitely. One that works for some people is the 'One Thing' technique. Pick one thing you want achieve each day, and tell nobody about it. Keep a little journal of progress. Then set timer for ten minutes every hour, and ask yourself whether the phone is more important than what you' doing. Most times, turn it off. Then get a white noise app and set it to background sound. Listen to music with earphones if it helps. At the very least, close the window shades so the glare doesn't bother you. That's a great idea. Many universities offer study spaces after hours.",
